    "result_text": "Changing the sheet's today now writes one `SNAPSHOT name=<name> due-total=<due-total>` line per person, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**The change:**\n- **`sheet/TodayService.java`:** the change already took a rollup snapshot before moving the date. When the new date is different from the current one, the SNAPSHOT lines are now written from that earlier snapshot. That puts them before any period closes and before the change's ROLLUP/TOTALS lines.\n- **`rollup/RollupService.java`:** a new `recordSnapshot` method writes the lines in list order (the order people were added), with the due-total as it stood on the day being left, `n/a` included. Lines are written only when the change commits, so a refused change writes nothing.\n\n**Decisions you may want to check:**\n- **Same date:** setting today to the date it already has writes no SNAPSHOT lines, since today hasn't changed. The tests never do this.\n- **Delegation:** SNAPSHOT lines get the usual `for=<steward>` ending when the user is acting by delegation, like every other line except ROLLUP and TOTALS.\n\n**Something else I had to fix:** once the SNAPSHOT lines were in, the last test got further and failed on an existing `PERSON_EDITED` line. It was written as `... grade=A terms= for=wes`, but the test expects `for=wes` straight after the grade. The audit service always added `for=` at the very end, after the person's trailing `terms=` field. I added a `recordOnCommit(record, trailing)` overload in `Audit.java` so extra fields can go after `for=`, and `PersonService` now passes `terms=` that way. I kept the existing rule of writing an empty `terms=` when the field is submitted blank, because the code's own comments say it's intended. The only difference is that `terms=` now comes after `for=` on delegated edits.",
